# Highest build number uploaded to App Store Connect outside Xcode Cloud (Fastlane
# timestamps, %Y%m%d%H%M), per platform and marketing version
# (CFBundleShortVersionString). ci_pre_xcodebuild.sh refuses Xcode Cloud archives
# that would not be above these: macOS must beat every macOS entry whatever the
# version; iOS, tvOS and visionOS must beat the entry for the version they build,
# and a version without an entry may start from small Xcode Cloud numbers.
# Record every later Fastlane upload here in a PR right after the upload, before
# the next Xcode Cloud archive. See docs/release/distribution.md#build-numbers.
#
# Format: <platform> <marketing-version> <build-number>, one entry per line
# platform: ios (iPhone, iPad and the embedded watch app), macos, tvos, visionos
# marketing-version: exactly x.y.z, three numbers without leading zeros (1.0.0,
#   not 1.0 or 01.0.0), matching MARKETING_VERSION in the project, which must
#   use the same form
# build-number: positive integer without leading zeros
ios 1.0.0 202610271751
macos 1.0.0 202610271753
tvos 1.0.0 202610271756
visionos 1.0.0 202610271757
